### `scripts/testing/run-native-sauce.sh`

This earlier teaching wrapper assumes relative runner paths for its configuration. Platform Engineering can maintain it as shared tooling if the approved integration uses it. Confirm the actual runtime location and invocation before use. The custom-step approach can supply the same automation without this wrapper. It requires an installed CLI and separate app/test storage references.

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
set +x
: "${SAUCE_USERNAME:?Protected Sauce identity required}"
: "${SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY:?Protected Sauce access key required}"
: "${MOBILE_NATIVE_FRAMEWORK:?espresso or xcuitest required}"
: "${MOBILE_NATIVE_APP_REF:?Verified current app storage reference required}"
: "${MOBILE_NATIVE_TEST_REF:?Verified matching test runner storage reference required}"
: "${MOBILE_SAUCE_REGION:?Approved Sauce region required}"
: "${MOBILE_TEST_BUILD_LABEL:?Sanitized build correlation label required}"
case "$MOBILE_SAUCE_REGION" in
  us-west-1|eu-central-1) ;;
  *) printf "%s\n" "Use a supported approved native-runner region." >&2; exit 1 ;;
esac
for reference in "$MOBILE_NATIVE_APP_REF" "$MOBILE_NATIVE_TEST_REF"; do
  case "$reference" in
    storage:*) [[ -n "${reference#storage:}" ]] || exit 1 ;;
    *) exit 1 ;;
  esac
  case "$reference" in
    *[[:space:]]*|*'<'*|*'>'*|*REPLACE_WITH_*)
      printf "%s\n" "Set verified app/test storage references before dispatch." >&2
      exit 1
      ;;
  esac
done
[[ "$MOBILE_NATIVE_APP_REF" != "$MOBILE_NATIVE_TEST_REF" ]] || exit 1
case "$MOBILE_NATIVE_FRAMEWORK" in
  espresso)
    : "${MOBILE_ANDROID_OS:?Approved Android OS target required}"
    config='.sauce/espresso.yml'
    ;;
  xcuitest)
    : "${MOBILE_IOS_OS:?Approved iOS OS target required}"
    config='.sauce/xcuitest.yml'
    ;;
  *) exit 1 ;;
esac
test -s "$config"
command -v saucectl >/dev/null
exec saucectl run --config "$config"
```

| Example input | Value to supply |
|---|---|
| `MOBILE_NATIVE_FRAMEWORK` | `espresso` or `xcuitest`. |
| `MOBILE_NATIVE_APP_REF` | Verified current `storage:<app ID>`. |
| `MOBILE_NATIVE_TEST_REF` | Verified matching `storage:<test package ID>`. |
| `MOBILE_SAUCE_REGION` | Approved compatible region. |
| `MOBILE_ANDROID_OS` / `MOBILE_IOS_OS` | Approved OS version for the selected suite. |
| `MOBILE_TEST_BUILD_LABEL` | Sanitized source/build correlation label. |

This wrapper is a teaching adaptation, with added checks for the documented native regions and unresolved/whitespace-containing storage references. It checks input shape and file availability. The approved adapter must also verify the actual remote package identity and bytes. Use the detailed `.sauce/espresso.yml` or `.sauce/xcuitest.yml` above when this wrapper is selected.

## 7. Understand the standalone upload and runner scripts

The latest reference also supplies direct upload and execution scripts. Choose one approved upload path. If the private workflow uploads the packages, a separate upload command must be coordinated with that implementation.

### Supplied application upload script

The following script is unchanged. It uploads `$APP_PATH` to the US West Storage API and reads `.item.id` from its response.

```bash
RESPONSE=$(curl -u "$SAUCE_USERNAME:$SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY" \
  --location \
  --request POST 'https://api.us-west-1.saucelabs.com/v1/storage/upload' \
  -F "payload=@$APP_PATH" \
  -F "name=$(basename "$APP_PATH")")

APP_ID=$(echo "$RESPONSE" | jq -r '.item.id')
envman add --key SAUCE_APP_ID --value "$APP_ID"
echo "Uploaded app to Sauce Labs. Storage ID: $APP_ID"
```

Before using this excerpt, confirm the input file, account region, response validation, and exact storage identity. The script omits complete HTTP/error handling. It also does not upload a matching test package or validate the result against the registered application identity.

`envman add` exposes the ID through the running workflow environment. Separate workflow VMs need the approved output handoff. For an ambiguous upload result, inspect exact remote state before repeating the write.

